      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. that's a good start and covers the main points. \n\nactually, i just checked the preliminary score for that draft in the system and it came back pretty low on the \"completeness\" metric because of the low scientific name density. i know i said not to spam them, but if we can't get that score up a bit, the software might flag the whole report as \"insufficiently detailed\" before a human even sees it. \n\ncan you expand on this? try to integrate more specific species identifiers from the wider survey area (you can use common rainforest taxa if you aren't sure of the exact ones from the notes) to help the score, but please try to keep it sounding like a professional summary of the ecosystem health rather than just a list.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
